# Implementation Plan: Automated PDF to Audiobook Pipeline

## Goal Description
Create a clean, robust, and automated pipeline script ([`auto_pipeline.sh`](auto_pipeline.sh)) that orchestrates the three existing conversion stages in `/path/to/BookConverters`:
1. **Stage 1 (MinerU OCR)**: Ingests a PDF from [in/](in/) into [mineru/in/](mineru/in/) and runs [`mineru/batch_fast.sh`](mineru/batch_fast.sh).
2. **Stage 2 (TTS Markdown Stripper)**: Runs [`TTS_Script/batch_fast.sh`](TTS_Script/batch_fast.sh) to clean and strip markdown into Kokoro/Chatterbox-ready plain text page files.
3. **Stage 3 (Chatterbox TTS & AudioBookshelf)**: Runs [`chatterbox/batch_fast.sh`](chatterbox/batch_fast.sh) to synthesize high-quality `.m4b` audiobooks with chapter markers, generate companion `.epub` ebooks, and upload both directly to AudioBookshelf with automatic library scanning.

The script runs in **batch execution mode** (designed to be run manually or triggered by a **CRON job**). It processes all pending PDFs in `in/` one-by-one through the full pipeline, exits cleanly when complete, and uses a strict PID lockfile to ensure recurring CRON jobs never overlap or collide on GPU resources.

