## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Pre-existing files in pipeline**:
> 1. In [mineru/out/](mineru/out/), there are currently **4 completed OCR books** from earlier runs (`AI and ML for Coders in PyTorch`, `AI and Machine Learning for Coders`, `Essential Math for AI`, `The Lazy Dungeon Master`).
> 2. In [mineru/in/](mineru/in/), there is a leftover **0-byte empty file** (`Basic_Electrical_and_Electronics_Engineering.pdf`), which would cause `mineru/batch_fast.sh` to fail if not cleaned up.
>
> **Proposed Behavior**:
> - The pipeline will automatically remove or quarantine 0-byte corrupt files before starting.
> - By default, the pipeline will feature a **backlog draining phase** on startup: if books are already sitting in `mineru/out/` or `TTS_Script/out/`, it will complete stages 2 & 3 for them before pulling new PDFs from `in/`, avoiding duplicate OCR compute. (Can be disabled with `--no-drain`).

> [!NOTE]
> **Single-Book Sequential Flow**:
> The pipeline processes **one PDF at a time** through Stages 1 &rarr; 2 &rarr; 3 &rarr; AudioBookshelf upload. This minimizes disk space usage (temporary page images and audio chunks are cleaned up per book), provides early delivery into AudioBookshelf as each book finishes, and ensures failures on one book do not block others.

